If the input data is a list or a dictionary, it recursively calls itself with each element of the list or value of the dictionary.

Finally, if the input data is not any of the above types, it raises a `TypeError` exception indicating that the type is not supported.

It's important to note that this function assumes that the input data is always valid and will not perform any error handling or validation.

