This method is a part of the MultiView class in Pyramid. It allows you to check if a certain view is permitted based on its context and request. This method iterates over all the views in the multi-view and checks for each one if it has the `__permitted__` attribute. If a view does not have this attribute, it means that it can be accessed regardless of the context or request, so we return `True`. 
In case the `__permitted__` attribute is set to `False`, it means that the view is not permitted for this particular context and request combination. In this case, the method returns `False`.

